      <title>Accretion Structures</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/research/accretion-structures/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/research/accretion-structures/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;page-loader&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;canvas id=&#34;solar-loader&#34;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;loader-overlay&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p id=&#34;astro-fact-text&#34; class=&#34;loader-fact&#34;&gt;Did You Know?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&#34;white-flash&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;main class=&#34;research-page&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;section class=&#34;section research-article-section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;container&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;section-shell&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;research-page-topbar&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;a class=&#34;back-link&#34; href=&#34;//localhost:1313/#research&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-arrow-left&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Back to Research&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button id=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; class=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; aria-label=&#34;Toggle theme&#34;&gt;☀️&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;section-head&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h2 id=&#34;research-page-title&#34;&gt;Accretion Structures&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h3 class=&#34;muted&#34; id=&#34;research-page-subtitle&#34;&gt;Accretion disks, mass transfer, and compact-object environments.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;article id=&#34;research-content&#34; class=&#34;card markdown-body research-article-card&#34;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Accretion Structures&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Accretion processes occur when matter falls onto compact astrophysical objects such as black holes, neutron stars, or young stars.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Research Questions&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How do accretion disks transport angular momentum?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;What mechanisms trigger accretion outbursts?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How does magnetic activity affect disk evolution?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Physical Processes&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Magnetohydrodynamics&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Disk turbulence&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Radiative transfer&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Observational Signatures&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Accretion structures can be studied through:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Chemical Tagging</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/research/chemical-tagging/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/research/chemical-tagging/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;page-loader&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;canvas id=&#34;solar-loader&#34;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;loader-overlay&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p id=&#34;astro-fact-text&#34; class=&#34;loader-fact&#34;&gt;Did You Know?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&#34;white-flash&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;main class=&#34;research-page&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;section class=&#34;section research-article-section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;container&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;section-shell&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;research-page-topbar&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;a class=&#34;back-link&#34; href=&#34;//localhost:1313/#research&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-arrow-left&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Back to Research&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button id=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; class=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; aria-label=&#34;Toggle theme&#34;&gt;☀️&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;section-head&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h2 id=&#34;research-page-title&#34;&gt;Chemical Tagging&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h3 class=&#34;muted&#34; id=&#34;research-page-subtitle&#34;&gt;Tracing stellar origins and shared formation environments through abundance patterns.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;article id=&#34;research-content&#34; class=&#34;card markdown-body research-article-card&#34;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Chemical Tagging&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Chemical tagging is a technique used to identify groups of stars that formed together in the same molecular cloud by comparing their chemical abundance patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Key Idea&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Stars born in the same stellar nursery share nearly identical chemical compositions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Scientific Importance&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Chemical tagging helps astronomers:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Identify disrupted star clusters&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Reconstruct the Milky Way&amp;#x27;s formation history&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Understand galactic chemical evolution&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Data Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;High-resolution spectroscopy&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Precise abundance measurements&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Future Work&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Combining chemical tagging with Gaia kinematic data to trace stellar migration in the Galactic disk.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Galactic Archaeology</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/research/galactic-archaeology/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/research/galactic-archaeology/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;page-loader&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;canvas id=&#34;solar-loader&#34;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;loader-overlay&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p id=&#34;astro-fact-text&#34; class=&#34;loader-fact&#34;&gt;Did You Know?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&#34;white-flash&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;main class=&#34;research-page&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;section class=&#34;section research-article-section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;container&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;section-shell&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;research-page-topbar&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;a class=&#34;back-link&#34; href=&#34;//localhost:1313/#research&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-arrow-left&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Back to Research&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button id=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; class=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; aria-label=&#34;Toggle theme&#34;&gt;☀️&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;section-head&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h2 id=&#34;research-page-title&#34;&gt;Galactic Archaeology&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h3 class=&#34;muted&#34; id=&#34;research-page-subtitle&#34;&gt;Formation history of the Milky Way through stellar populations and chemical evolution.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;article id=&#34;research-content&#34; class=&#34;card markdown-body research-article-card&#34;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Galactic Archaeology&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Galactic archaeology studies the formation history of galaxies by analyzing the chemical and dynamical properties of stars.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Key Questions&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How did the Milky Way form?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;What are the origins of stellar populations?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Can we trace ancient merger events?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Methods&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Stellar spectroscopy&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Chemical abundance analysis&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Stellar kinematics&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Large survey data analysis&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Tools&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Python&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Astropy&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Machine learning models&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/section&gt;&#xA;&lt;/main&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script defer src=&#34;//localhost:1313/js/astro-facts.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script defer src=&#34;//localhost:1313/js/solar-loader.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script defer src=&#34;//localhost:1313/js/main.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script defer src=&#34;//localhost:1313/js/site-init.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Machine Learning for Stellar Spectroscopy</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/research/ml-spectroscopy/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/research/ml-spectroscopy/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;page-loader&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;canvas id=&#34;solar-loader&#34;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;loader-overlay&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p id=&#34;astro-fact-text&#34; class=&#34;loader-fact&#34;&gt;Did You Know?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&#34;white-flash&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;main class=&#34;research-page&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;section class=&#34;section research-article-section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;container&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;section-shell&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;research-page-topbar&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;a class=&#34;back-link&#34; href=&#34;//localhost:1313/#research&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-arrow-left&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span&gt;Back to Research&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;          &lt;button id=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; class=&#34;theme-toggle&#34; aria-label=&#34;Toggle theme&#34;&gt;☀️&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;section-head&#34;&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h2 id=&#34;research-page-title&#34;&gt;Machine Learning for Stellar Spectroscopy&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;          &lt;h3 class=&#34;muted&#34; id=&#34;research-page-subtitle&#34;&gt;Data-driven methods for extracting stellar parameters and abundance information.&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;        &lt;article id=&#34;research-content&#34; class=&#34;card markdown-body research-article-card&#34;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Machine Learning for Stellar Spectroscopy&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Machine learning techniques are increasingly used to analyze large spectroscopic datasets and extract stellar parameters efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Research Goals&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Predict stellar temperature, gravity, and metallicity&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Identify unusual stellar spectra&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Automate spectral classification&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Techniques Used&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Neural networks&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Random forests&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Dimensionality reduction (PCA, t-SNE)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Applications&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Machine learning models can process millions of stellar spectra from modern surveys and identify patterns that may be difficult to detect with traditional methods.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
